/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - An NMOS conducts when electrons are pulled through a p-type body toward an n+ drain.
   - The well-substrate junction must stay reverse biased.
   - In a p-well process the wafer starts n-type.
   - Most digital CMOS uses n-well.
*/
